--   An intermediate lemma of the split of OpenAI's proof of `OAI.TotientAsymptotic.coefficient_nonnegative`, `OAI.TotientAsymptotic.totient_asymptotic_formula`, `OAI.TotientAsymptotic.weighted_totient_asymptotic` and `OAI.TotientAsymptotic.weighted_totient_one_two`, carved from OpenAI's openai/math development for this platform. The statement and its proof are OpenAI's (OpenAI, *An asymptotic formula for the number of totients (result family 024)*, OpenAI Math Release, September 25, 2026, result family 24, [github.com/openai/math](https://github.com/openai/math), Apache License 2.0); in Lean it is the declaration `OAI.TotientAsymptotic.candidate_mass_normalized` of [lean/OAI/NumberTheory/TotientAsymptotic/WeightedMass.lean](https://github.com/openai/math/blob/7ef5c0cc5ca4b0e072b7a050fca09ab24bc6fa3a/lean/OAI/NumberTheory/TotientAsymptotic/WeightedMass.lean) at commit 7ef5c0c, ported to Lean 4.33.1 and Mathlib 0df444a.
--
--   **The statement**, as published (namespace `OAI.TotientAsymptotic`, with `open scoped BigOperators Topology Classical`, `open Filter`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem candidate_mass_normalized (hpnt : PrimeNumberTheoremInput)
--       (hbox : FordUnitPrimeBoxInput) (hren : FordRenewalInput) (hmertens : MertensProductInput)
--       (k : ℕ) (hk : 1 ≤ k) :
--       ∃ δ : ℕ → ℝ, Tendsto δ atTop (nhds 0) ∧
--         ∀ᶠ H : ℕ in atTop, ∀ ε : ℝ, 0 < ε → ∀ᶠ x : ℝ in atTop,
--           |((candidateTuples x H k).card : ℝ)/tupleNormalization x-
